## Why SEO matters for small businesses

Most customers search on Google before they decide to buy. If your business does not show up, those customers go to a competitor instead. Good SEO makes sure people in your area find you first.

### 1. Target local keywords

Use phrases your customers actually type, like your city name and "near me". For example, a bakery in Faridabad should target "best bakery in Faridabad" rather than just "bakery".

### 2. Write helpful content

Answer the real questions your customers ask. Helpful articles build trust and bring in steady traffic from search.

### 3. Speed up your website

A slow website loses visitors and rankings. Compress images and keep your pages light.

### 4. Get listed on Google Business Profile

This is one of the fastest ways for local businesses to appear in search and maps.

### 5. Earn quality backlinks

When other trusted websites link to you, Google trusts you more. Focus on a few good links rather than many weak ones.
